# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages.
# Format: path pattern, headers indented below it.
#
# On the CSP decision: script-src/style-src need 'unsafe-inline', because
# the whole app is deliberately built as a single file with inline
# <style>/<script> (no external files, no frameworks). The clean
# alternative would be a SHA-256 hash per inline block — but those would
# need recomputing and re-entering here on EVERY code change, or the page
# silently breaks. For a one-person project that risk/maintenance ratio is
# bad. The rest of the CSP therefore stays deliberately tight: no external
# scripts, no third-party connection targets, no embedding in other sites.
#
# connect-src lists the targets actually used: our own proxy (WebUntis +
# Mensamax go through it) and ccCampus (runs directly from the browser for
# technical reasons). ccCampus runs under several domains of the same
# provider (same software, same "/ordering/" path) — mbs5online.de and the
# shorter mbs5.de. This list has to match CCCAMPUS_ALLOWED_DOMAINS in
# web/index.html — entering a domain only here or only there isn't enough,
# both checks need to know about it. Further domains of the same provider
# aren't ruled out; if another one shows up, add it here AND there.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://stundenplan-proxy.bluedemann.workers.dev https://*.mbs5online.de https://*.mbs5.de; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
